{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>Adjacent to \"When you come into your fellow's vineyard\" — לנדר</b>. Hint: סחור סחור לכרמא לא תקרב (go around, go around — do not approach the vineyard). For if he took a nazirite vow, he must not hire himself out for vineyard work. Therefore Scripture placed vineyard before field, which is not the normal order." "<b>\"You shall not give\"</b> — and adjacent to it: \"When you come into your fellow's standing grain.\" Hint: sometimes \"you shall not give\" — even into your mouth, such as one who works in this species and does not eat of another species."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:10:29.840526334Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}